    "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Bard’s are heralds of the awe-inspiring beauty of creation. While the painter and sculptor decorate space, a Bard decorates time.</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Iconic Bards</strong></b></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Edward Chris von Muir, Final Fantasy IV</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Jaskier, The Witcher</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Kvothe, The Kingkiller Chronicle</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">• Sylvando, Dragon Quest XI</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Playing Bards</strong></b></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">The bard is a mid-defense, high-support class with a focus on optimizing your Group’s d20 rolls. It’s recommended that you avoid melee on most Bard builds.</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Action:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"> Virtuoso</span></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Move:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"> Midline/Backline</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Training:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"> Finesse, Influence, Performance</span></p>",
